+# Design
+
+## Context
+
+The repository has no source yet (`tsconfig.json` includes `src`, ESM/NodeNext, strict; tests run with `node --test`). The library has no runtime dependencies. Requirements are in `specs/json-pointer/spec.md`.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:**
+- A small pure function, with an internal split between parsing a pointer into tokens and walking the document, so later features can reuse the parser.
+
+**Non-Goals:**
+- URI fragment form, mutation, or exposing the parser publicly yet.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- **Parse then walk.** Validate the whole pointer first (so an invalid pointer throws even if the document would fail earlier), then resolve token by token. Alternative: validate lazily — rejected as it makes errors depend on the document.
+- **Own-property lookup** via `Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call`, so prototype keys are never reached. Array indices checked with `/^(0|[1-9][0-9]*)$/` and `< length`.
+- **Token decoding** by splitting on `/` and replacing `~1` then `~0` in a single regex pass (`/~([01])/` with a mapper), after checking no `~` is followed by anything else.
+- Source layout: implementation lives in `src/index.ts` for now (no tsc available; Node runs `.ts` via type stripping, which cannot resolve `./x.js` imports to `.ts`). Tests in `test/` import `../src/index.ts`.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- [Tests are TypeScript but only `node --test` is available] → rely on Node 22 type stripping; use only erasable TS syntax.
