+## Why
+
+Our services need one standard way to refer to a value inside a JSON document. RFC 6901 (JSON Pointer) is the published standard for it, and later features of this library will build on it.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `resolvePointer(document, pointer)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, which returns the value a JSON Pointer string refers to.
+- It throws an error when the pointer is not a valid JSON Pointer, or when it does not resolve to a value of the document.
+- Behaviour follows RFC 6901 exactly (syntax, `~0`/`~1` escaping, array index rules, the `-` token).
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-pointer`: parsing and resolving RFC 6901 JSON Pointers against a JSON document.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+None.
+
+## Impact
+
+- New code in `src/` (the project has no source yet) and tests; no dependencies added.
+- New public API surface of the library, which other projects import.
+- Out of scope: the URI fragment representation (RFC 6901 section 6), and modifying documents.
